  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4d08-c639-04d4-a017" name="Nubian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #107 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Nubia occupies the upper reaches of the Nile above upper Egypt and was the source of destructive raids upon the civilised areas. Egypt gradually pushed its border further up river and Nubia was considered annexed by 1900 BC, lost again during the Hyksos invasions and reconquered by 1100 BC, although the tribes seem to have thought differently and continued to cause trouble for hundreds of years. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Nubian]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 67%
  Characters: up to 33% Infantry: At least 67%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
